Troubleshooting Tips
Permission Errors:

Use sudo for commands requiring root access (iptables, systemctl)
Ensure log directories are writable: chmod 755 logs/
Import Errors:

Verify sys.path.append() points to correct directory
Check that base_playbook.py exists and is executable
Command Execution Failures:

Test commands manually first: netstat -tuln, ps aux
Check command syntax in execute_command() method
Verify timeout settings for long-running commands
No Threats Detected:

Create test suspicious files in /tmp
Simulate network connections with curl or netcat
Check detection thresholds in your code
Conclusion
In this lab, you developed automated SOC playbooks for incident response. You created a reusable framework, implemented malware detection with quarantine capabilities, built network intrusion response with IP blocking, and developed system isolation procedures with evidence collection. These playbooks form the foundation of automated security operations, enabling rapid response to security incidents while maintaining detailed audit trails. Practice extending these playbooks with additional detection rules, notification integrations, and remediation actions to build a comprehensive SOC automation platform.
